# Hardware profiles

The client must stay playable on modest GPUs and on 4K screens. Quality is a profile, not a fixed target.

Scale cost through `ChessGraphicsSettings` in `src/renderer/graphics/chessGraphicsSettings.ts`. Presets already exist: Fluide, Équilibré, Qualité, Natif. The stored default is `FLUID_GRAPHICS` (1080p, textures 256, no ambient occlusion, no reflections, no bloom).

A new GPU cost — pass, shadow, texture size, resolution — is off in Fluide and opt-in on the higher presets. Gate it in `gamePassNames` or `pieceTextureSize`. Do not run it unconditionally.

```typescript
// ❌ heavy pass always in the frame
names.push('05_SSR_Floor', '05b_SSR_Composite');

// ✅ same pass, only when the active profile asks for it
if (value.reflections) names.push('05_SSR_Floor', '05b_SSR_Composite');
```

Internal resolution is capped (`gameSurfacePixels`). Do not size a framebuffer from `window.devicePixelRatio` alone. Chess rules, input, and audio do not depend on a graphics preset.

Add a failing test in `tests/chessGraphics.test.ts` before changing a preset, a cap, or a pass list.
